Talos kernel patch for Radxa TACO boards (talos-builds, kernels/rpi_cm-radxa_taco/patches).

Raspberry Pi's partial revert of upstream 105c42566a55 ("ata: ahci: force 32-bit DMA for
JMicron JMB582/JMB585"), as carried in raspberrypi/linux rpi-6.18.y since 2026-05-22
(commit 40116166e8e7, pull request #7393). On a BCM2712 (CM5) the PCIe controller has no
usable window below 4 GB, so the forced 32-bit DMA mask makes the JMB585 fail to probe
(error -12) and no SATA disk appears. Every inbound DMA address on a Pi 5 is above 4 GB
anyway, and the controller works with 64-bit DMA there. Evidence: kernels/rpi_cm-radxa_taco/README.md
(Raspberry Pi OS 6.18.50+rpt, which carries this patch, runs SATA and NVMe together on
the same board).

Applied by siderolabs/pkgs' kernel-build step (kernel/build/pkg.yaml applies every
kernel/build/patches/*.patch with patch -p1). Drop it once Talos's kernel carries a fix.

From: Phil Elwell <phil@raspberrypi.com>
Date: Fri, 22 May 2026 13:36:02 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Partially revert "ata: ahci: force 32-bit DMA for JMicron
 JMB582/JMB585"

This partially reverts commit 105c42566a550e2d05fc14f763216a8765ee5d0e.

Between [1] and this partial reversion, all users of the JMB582/JMB585
on Raspberry Pi 5 have been forced to use the pcie-32bit-dma overlay.

The reasoning behind the patch is either inherently flawed or does not
apply on a Pi 5, since all inbound memory accesses are by default above
4GB and yet seem to work.

See: https://github.com/raspberrypi/linux/issues/7355
     https://forums.raspberrypi.com/viewtopic.php?p=2374573&sid=a9d90a55d42694d4f24bf03946e44a4f#p2374573

Signed-off-by: Phil Elwell <phil@raspberrypi.com>

[1] commit 105c42566a55 ("ata: ahci: force 32-bit DMA for JMicron JMB582/JMB585")
---
 drivers/ata/ahci.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/ata/ahci.c b/drivers/ata/ahci.c
index 1d73a53370cf3e..eb2d896daa6612 100644
--- a/drivers/ata/ahci.c
+++ b/drivers/ata/ahci.c
@@ -216,7 +216,7 @@ static const struct ata_port_info ahci_port_info[] = {
 	/* JMicron JMB582/585: 64-bit DMA is broken, force 32-bit */
 	[board_ahci_jmb585] = {
 		AHCI_HFLAGS	(AHCI_HFLAG_IGN_IRQ_IF_ERR |
-				 AHCI_HFLAG_32BIT_ONLY),
+				 0*AHCI_HFLAG_32BIT_ONLY),
 		.flags		= AHCI_FLAG_COMMON,
 		.pio_mask	= ATA_PIO4,
 		.udma_mask	= ATA_UDMA6,
